# Working here from Antigravity

{% if use_claude_code %}
This project is set up for Claude Code and Antigravity at the same time. `CLAUDE.md`,
`.claude/skills/` and `.claude/agents/` are the one source of instructions for both; `.agents/`
only adapts them. Never edit `.claude/` to suit Antigravity: those files come from the copier
template (`.copier-answers.yml`) and a Claude Code session reads them too.
{% else %}
This project's instructions are written in Claude Code's layout: `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/skills/`,
`.claude/agents/` and `.claude/hooks/` are their one source, and `.agents/` only adapts them for
Antigravity. Change them there, not here: they come from the copier template
(`.copier-answers.yml`).
{% endif %}

## Reading Claude-flavoured instructions

Skills and agents name Claude Code tools. Use the Antigravity equivalent:

| Claude Code | Antigravity |
| --- | --- |
| Bash (`run_in_background`) | `run_command` (then `manage_task`) |
| Read / Grep / Glob | `view_file` / `grep_search` / `find_by_name` |
| Edit, MultiEdit / Write | `replace_file_content` / `write_to_file` |
| WebFetch / WebSearch | `read_url_content` / `search_web` |
| Skill tool, `/<name>` | the skill of the same name (`.claude/skills/<name>`, loaded via `.agents/skills.json`) |
| Agent tool, `subagent_type: X` | `invoke_subagent` with the custom agent X (`.agents/agents/`: dev, review, documenter, verify) |
| SendMessage into a running agent | `send_message` |
| AskUserQuestion | `ask_question` |
| TaskCreate / TaskUpdate | your own plan; nothing to call |

- `$ARGUMENTS` in a skill is the text the user typed after `/<name>`.
- `${{ project_dir_var }}` is the project root (the folder holding `.copier-answers.yml`).

## Claude-only pieces and what to do instead

{% if status_mcp == 'teams' %}
- **Teams / Microsoft 365** (`mcp__claude_ai_Microsoft_365__*`, `mcp__m365__*`): here Teams goes
  through the `teams-mcp` plugin (`.agents/plugins/teams-mcp/`, `okolovmark/teams-mcp#stable`):
  `auth_status` / `get_current_user`, `search_users`, `list_chats`, `create_chat`,
  `send_chat_message` / `send_channel_message` with `format: "markdown"`, `get_chat_messages`, and
  inline `@Full Name` with `mentions: [{mention, userId}]`. If `auth_status` is not the user's
  account, run `npx -y git+https://github.com/okolovmark/teams-mcp.git#stable authenticate` (or
  ask the user to authenticate) and re-check before sending.
{% endif %}
{% if tickets_mcp == 'odoo' %}
- **Odoo production connector** (the "Odoo connector" the skills call): available only when an
  Odoo MCP plugin under `.agents/plugins/` is enabled and signed in. Without it, ask; never swap
  in an ssh + odoo shell read the skill did not ask for.
{% endif %}
{% if use_pipeline and custom_repo_name %}
- **pipeline-gates** (`mcp__pipeline-gates__*`): enforced here by `.agents/hooks/claude_hook.py`
  and the `Pipeline` sidecar panel (`.agents/plugins/pipeline-gates/`, `[Pipeline](sidecar://pipeline-gates/panel/)`).
  Use `python3 .agents/hooks/claude_hook.py pipeline-gate phase <0..7> [TASK]` (or the panel UI) to
  advance phases and `pipeline-gate qc-verdict <pass|blocking> <summary>` to record the QC verdict:
  no `dev` agent and no worktree edit before
{% if status_mcp == 'teams' %}
  the Teams status is sent and
{% endif %}
  the grill gate is confirmed; no `gh pr create` before a `review` agent and a
  green test run (more than 0 tests) since the last code change; a fourth fix round only when the
  user grants `+3 rounds` in the panel, each round to a fresh `dev` agent.
{% endif %}
{% if prod_ssh_host and custom_repo_name %}
- **deploy-watch** (`mcp__deploy-watch__schedule_check`): schedule the T+60 re-check with the
  `schedule` tool (3600 s, the exact re-check commands as its prompt) and tell the user how to
  cancel it.
{% endif %}
- **Claude in Chrome / Claude Browser**: use the browser subagent (`/browser`) for UI checks and
  the 375 px phone check.
{% if custom_repo_name %}
- **odoo-env-band**: ported as the `Odoo Env & Worktrees` sidecar panel (`.agents/plugins/odoo-env/`,
  `[Odoo Env & Worktrees](sidecar://odoo-env/panel/)`), or from the CLI via
  `bash .claude/skills/worktree-env/scripts/wt-list.sh`.
- **Status line, agent memory** (`.claude/agent-memory/`): Claude UI only. Never write into
  `.claude/agent-memory/`.
{% else %}
- **Status line, agent memory** (`.claude/agent-memory/`): Claude UI only. Never write into
