## Hooks and entire

`.agents/hooks.json` runs the Claude Code hooks from `.claude/hooks/` through
`.agents/hooks/claude_hook.py`, plus `entire` (`entire hooks antigravity ...` for the root repo and
{% if custom_repo_name %}
`.agents/hooks/entire-fanout.sh` for nested repos like `src/{{ custom_repo_name }}`).
{% else %}
`.agents/hooks/entire-fanout.sh` for nested repos under `src/`).
{% endif %}
{% else %}
## Hooks

`.agents/hooks.json` runs the Claude Code hooks from `.claude/hooks/` through
`.agents/hooks/claude_hook.py`.
{% endif %}

- A denial from `guard-bash` or `guard-readonly` is final: run nothing that routes around it.
{% if custom_repo_name %}
  Odoo core and OCA under `src/` are read-only; only `src/{{ custom_repo_name }}` is edited.
{% else %}
  Odoo core and the third-party repos under `src/` are read-only.
{% endif %}
- A denial starting `find-code nudge` or `ui-design:` is a one-time nudge: follow it, or re-run
{% if use_kb %}
  the call when it does not apply, and the retry passes. `kb truncation guard` fires every time:
  read the record whole, or add `# truncation-ok` to the command when cutting is really right.
  `kb task guard` fires every time too: a task is filed only after the user picked kb for it,
  and then the command carries `# user-picked-kb`.
{% else %}
  the call when it does not apply, and the retry passes.
{% endif %}
{% if use_entire %}
- `.entire/metadata/` is read-denied everywhere: it holds session transcripts.
{% endif %}
- **Terminal sandbox**: Antigravity's default command sandbox does not mount `/nix`,
  `~/.local/bin`, or `/run/user/$UID/bus`, and blocks network/loopback sockets. Either disable the
  terminal sandbox in Antigravity settings (`enableTerminalSandbox: false`), or use
  `BypassSandbox: true` when running Nix binaries (`odoo`, `uv`, `ruff`, `psql`), `kb`,
  `systemctl --user`, `wt-*.sh`, or `ssh`.

